          "input": {
            "claim_observed": "Baseline imports /source/sample.py directly and calls can_read: can_read(\"alice\",\"bob\",False) returns True, i.e. an authenticated non-owner is granted read on a non-public document, while can_read(\"bob\",\"bob\",False) and can_read(None,\"bob\",True) are True and can_read(None,\"bob\",False) is False — the owner parameter never constrains the result, so the detector reports claim_present true. The counterexample reads the same source text, substitutes the single returned expression `public or bool(requester)` with an owner-comparing expression, executes the patched module, and runs the identical detector: cross-tenant private read becomes False while owner and public reads remain True, so claim_present is false. The difference between the two runs isolates the missing requester == owner comparison in sample.py lines 1-2 as the cause of the broken access control.",
            "files": [
              {
                "path": "generated/probe_source.py",
                "utf8": "import importlib.util\nimport json\n\nSRC = \"/source/sample.py\"\n\nspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"sample_under_test\", SRC)\nmod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nspec.loader.exec_module(mod)\n\n# Contract (README): access only for public documents, or an authenticated\n# requester equal to owner.\ncross_tenant = bool(mod.can_read(\"alice\", \"bob\", False))\nowner_access = bool(mod.can_read(\"bob\", \"bob\", False))\npublic_access = bool(mod.can_read(None, \"bob\", True))\nanonymous_private = bool(mod.can_read(None, \"bob\", False))\n\n# Broken access control is present when a non-owner authenticated requester is\n# granted read on a non-public document while the legitimate cases still hold.\nclaim_present = cross_tenant and owner_access and public_access and not anonymous_private\n\nprint(json.dumps({\n    \"target\": SRC,\n    \"cross_tenant_private_read\": cross_tenant,\n    \"owner_private_read\": owner_access,\n    \"public_read\": public_access,\n    \"anonymous_private_read\": anonymous_private,\n    \"claim_present\": bool(claim_present),\n}, sort_keys=True))\n"
              },
              {
                "path": "generated/probe_patched.py",
                "utf8": "import json\n\nSRC = \"/source/sample.py\"\n\nwith open(SRC, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n    text = fh.read()\n\nVULN = \"    return public or bool(requester)\"\nFIX = \"    return bool(public) or (bool(requester) and requester == owner)\"\n\npatch_applied = VULN in text\npatched_text = text.replace(VULN, FIX, 1) if patch_applied else text\n\nns = {\"__name__\": \"sample_patched\"}\nexec(compile(patched_text, \"sample_patched.py\", \"exec\"), ns)\ncan_read = ns[\"can_read\"]\n\ncross_tenant = bool(can_read(\"alice\", \"bob\", False))\nowner_access = bool(can_read(\"bob\", \"bob\", False))\npublic_access = bool(can_read(None, \"bob\", True))\nanonymous_private = bool(can_read(None, \"bob\", False))\n\n# Same detector as the baseline probe, applied to the owner-comparing variant\n# built from the very same source text.\nclaim_present = cross_tenant and owner_access and public_access and not anonymous_private\n\nprint(json.dumps({\n    \"target\": SRC,\n    \"patch_applied\": patch_applied,\n    \"cross_tenant_private_read\": cross_tenant,\n    \"owner_private_read\": owner_access,\n    \"public_read\": public_access,\n    \"anonymous_private_read\": anonymous_private,\n    \"claim_present\": bool(claim_present),\n}, sort_keys=True))\n"
              }
            ],
            "item_id": "omission-1-f5201e5feb8fc093",
